\section{Validation overview}
The report separates four check families. A skipped check means that its
reference data, configuration, region, unit, or exact endpoint year was not
available; it is not counted as a pass.

<<overview, echo=FALSE, results='asis'>>=
render_table(validation_sections$overview, longtable = FALSE)
@

\section{Validation checks}
This section compares reported model values with the packaged 2024 benchmark
ranges derived from \texttt{validation-checks.csv}. Values inside the
published lower--upper range pass; values outside the range warn up to a 50\%
relative deviation from the central estimate and fail beyond it.

<<historical, echo=FALSE, results='asis'>>=
validation <- validation_sections$validation
validation_pass <- validation[validation$status == "pass", , drop = FALSE]
validation_other <- validation[validation$status != "pass", , drop = FALSE]

cat("\\subsection{Evaluated historical checks - Pass}\n\n")
if (nrow(validation_pass)) {
  render_placeholder_or_findings(validation_pass)
} else {
  cat("No evaluated historical numerical checks passed.\n\n")
}

cat("\\subsection{Evaluated historical checks - Warnings, fails and NAs}\n\n")
if (!nrow(validation_other)) {
  cat("All evaluated historical numerical checks passed.\n\n")
} else {
  render_placeholder_or_findings(validation_other)
}
@

\section{Policy checks}
Policy checks evaluate exact individual-country regions from the Climate Policy
Modelling Protocol. The source for all checks in this section is Dafnomilis, I.,
Hooijschuur, E., Schmidt Tagomori, I., van Soest, H., Roelfsema, M.\ \& den
Elzen, M. (2026), \textit{Climate Policy Modelling Protocol} [Dataset], Zenodo,
\href{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20848687}{Zenodo record}.
Only protocol regions available directly in OPEN-PROM are included; CHN is
mapped explicitly to CHA. Policy years use the nearest available model year up
to two years away, with no interpolation. A configured target can be an absolute maximum
or minimum, or a minimum/maximum reduction or increase relative to a specified
baseline year. For Japan's technology-specific electricity targets, validation
derives the required share internally as source generation divided by total
electricity generation. These temporary shares are not added to the Postprom
report; its existing aggregate renewables-share indicator remains unchanged.
Pass is under 10\%, warning until 50\% and fail is larger than 50\%.

<<policies, echo=FALSE, results='asis'>>=
render_placeholder_or_findings(
  validation_sections$policies,
  relative_deviation = FALSE,
  include_source = FALSE
)
@

\section{Indicators check}
These checks use the indicators already calculated by
\texttt{reportIndicators()}. Pass is under 10\%, warning until 50\% and fail is larger than 50\%.  

<<indicators, echo=FALSE, results='asis'>>=
indicator_result <- validation_sections$indicators
cat("\\subsection{Summary}\n\n")
render_table(indicator_result$summary, longtable = FALSE)

benchmark <- indicatorFindingsForPdf(indicator_result)
benchmark <- benchmark[
  benchmark$check_id %in% indicator_result$findings$check_id[
    indicator_result$findings$check_type %in% c("level", "cagr")
  ] & benchmark$status == "pass",
  ,
  drop = FALSE
]
cat("\\subsection{Evaluated benchmarks - Pass}\n\n")
if (nrow(benchmark)) {
  render_table(prepare_findings(benchmark))
} else {
  cat("No evaluated indicator benchmarks passed.\n\n")
}

indicator_exceptions <- indicatorFindingsForPdf(indicator_result)
indicator_exceptions <- indicator_exceptions[
  indicator_exceptions$status != "pass", , drop = FALSE
]
cat("\\subsection{Evaluated benchmarks - Warnings, fails and NAs}\n\n")
if (!nrow(indicator_exceptions)) {
  cat("All evaluated indicator checks passed.\n\n")
} else {
  render_table(prepare_findings(indicator_exceptions))
}
@

\section{Long term checks}
This section compares model results with targets derived from
\texttt{quantified\_longterm\_trends.md} which are based on the current policies document. Checks can compare annualized
trends, cumulative changes, or endpoint levels. Exact configured years are
required and no interpolation is performed. EU27 targets use the aggregate
\texttt{EU} report region rather than separate member-state results. Pass is under 10\%, warning until 50\% and fail is larger than 50\%.

<<long_term, echo=FALSE, results='asis'>>=
long_term <- validation_sections$long_term
long_term_pass <- long_term[long_term$status == "pass", , drop = FALSE]
long_term_other <- long_term[long_term$status != "pass", , drop = FALSE]

cat("\\subsection{Evaluated long-term checks - Pass}\n\n")
if (nrow(long_term_pass)) {
  render_table(prepare_findings(
    long_term_pass, include_source = FALSE
  ))
} else {
  cat("No evaluated long-term checks passed.\n\n")
}

cat("\\subsection{Evaluated long-term checks - Warnings, fails and NAs}\n\n")
if (!nrow(long_term_other)) {
  cat("All evaluated long-term checks passed.\n\n")
} else {
  render_placeholder_or_findings(
    long_term_other, include_source = FALSE
  )
}
@

